NAME
       blockdev - ask the kernel about a block device, or tell it to reread one

SYNOPSIS
       blockdev --getsize64 DEVICE
       blockdev --rereadpt DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       blockdev talks to the kernel's block device layer directly. It is run
       as root.

OPTIONS
       --getsize64
              Print the size of the device in bytes.

       --rereadpt
              Ask the kernel to read the partition table again, after a
              partitioning tool changed it. This fails if a partition of the
              disk is in use; partprobe is the usual alternative.

EXAMPLES
           blockdev --getsize64 /dev/vdb
           blockdev --rereadpt /dev/vdb

SEE ALSO
       lsblk(8), partprobe(8), fdisk(8)
